 <longdesc><para unique="1091851">Unpacks and interleaves the low-order data elements (bytes, words, doublewords, and quadwords) of the destina&#173;tion operand (first operand) and source operand (second operand) into the destination operand. (<link unique="1091853" linkend="#21211: 05_FigureFrame: Figure 3-15. PUNPCKHBW Instruction Operation" xrefstyle="FigureNum">Figure&#160;4&#8209;22</link> shows the unpack operation for bytes in 64-bit operands.). The high-order data elements are ignored.</para>
  <figure id="21211: 05_FigureFrame: Figure 3-15. PUNPCKHBW Instruction Operation"><title>PUNPCKLBW Instruction Operation Using 64-bit Operands</title>
   <mediaobject><imageobject><svg width="1000" height="257.58338271224136" viewBox="0 0 354.80736 91.39247999999999">
      <defs>
        <marker id="arrow" viewBox="0 0 6 6" refX="3" refY="3" markerWidth="9" markerHeight="9" orient="auto-start-reverse">
          <path d="M 0 0 L 6 3 L 0 6 L 1.5 3 z"/>
        </marker>
      </defs>
      <rect width="144.0" height="18.0" x="154.28448" y="68.32079999999999" style="stroke-width:0.5; stroke: #000000; fill: #ffffff;"/>
      <polyline points="190.12104,68.32079999999999 190.12104,86.3208" style="stroke-width:0.5; stroke: #000000; fill: #ffffff;"/>
      <polyline points="226.17504,68.32079999999999 226.17504,86.3208" style="stroke-width:0.5; stroke: #000000; fill: #ffffff;"/>
